  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nHigh pressure ridge over the southwestern US will keep Nevada dry\nthroughout the week. Dry and quiet pattern looks to anchor over \nthe Silver Stat this week as any active weather looks to stay well\nto the north. Along with that a warming trend will see \ntemperatures run about 10 degrees above normal for this time as \nhighs average in the low to mid 60s, with overnight lows in the \nupper 20s to 30s. Winds will be light to breezy in the afternoons \nrunning out of the W to SW at 5 to 15 MPH with gusts up to 25 MPH \npossible. However a upper trough passing to the north will act to \nincrease winds Saturday afternoon through Sunday evening, but only\nfor northern portions of Humboldt and Elko counties as winds will\npick up to 15 to 25 MPH with gusts up to 35 MPH possible. Monday \nthrough Friday of next week quiet conditions resume for the \nregion. Beginning next Saturday models hint at the possibility of \na strong upper trough that will try to push into Nevada. Although \nstill very early, there are hints of an atmospheric river \ncomponent with this system that long range models are picking up \non. So the possibility of a return of beneficial rain and snow \nwill need to be watch over the several days. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in upper ridge setting up over the great\nbasin lasting through Friday of next week which will bring dry \nconditions and light winds. \n\nThere is medium confidence for an upper level trough passage \nacross the Pacific northwest leading to increased winds across far\nnorthern Nevada Saturday into Sunday. \n     \nThere is low to low confidence of upper pattern evolution after \nFriday as models show a strong upper trough pushing into the \nwestern US.",
